<reference id="_Toc238560345" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 9: Three-level deep nested numbered list in a workflow</title>
   <shortdesc>Consider an alarm lifecycle workflow that contains stages, sub-stages, and detailed activities.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>Alarm</keyword>
        <keyword>workflow</keyword>
        <keyword>nested</keyword>
        <keyword>Evaluate</keyword>
        <keyword>Three</keyword>
        <keyword>level</keyword>
        <indexterm>Alarm</indexterm>
        <indexterm>workflow</indexterm>
        <indexterm>nested</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody><section><p>Consider an alarm lifecycle workflow that contains stages, sub-stages, and detailed activities.</p>
<table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Three-level deep nested numbered list (workflow)</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry> .md input </entry>
                     <entry> DITA output </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock># Alarm Lifecycle
  1. Alarm Detection
  1. Rule Evaluation
  1. Evaluate Thresholds
  2. Evaluate Conditions
  2. Alarm Creation
  2. Alarm Resolution</codeblock>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>&lt;concept id="alarm_lifecycle"&gt;     &lt;title&gt;Alarm Lifecycle&lt;/title&gt;     &lt;conbody&gt;         &lt;ol&gt;             &lt;li&gt;                 Alarm Detection                 &lt;ol&gt;                     &lt;li&gt;                         Rule Evaluation                         &lt;ol&gt;   &lt;li&gt;Evaluate Thresholds&lt;/li&gt;  &lt;li&gt;Evaluate Conditions&lt;/li&gt;                         &lt;/ol&gt;                     &lt;/li&gt;                     &lt;li&gt;Alarm Creation&lt;/li&gt;                 &lt;/ol&gt;             &lt;/li&gt;             &lt;li&gt;Alarm Resolution&lt;/li&gt;         &lt;/ol&gt;     &lt;/conbody&gt; &lt;/concept&gt;</codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
<p>
            <b>Result:</b> The content describes a workflow rather than a procedure, and all list levels are preserved as nested DITA ordered lists (<codeph>&lt;ol&gt;</codeph>).</p></section></refbody>
</reference>
